---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
const assets = [
 {name:'Mark', image:'/mark.svg', links:[['SVG','/mark.svg'],['PNG','/magpie-mark.png']]},
 {name:'Wordmark', image:'/wordmark.svg', links:[['SVG','/wordmark.svg']]},
 {name:'Avatar', image:'/brand/avatar-400.png', links:[['400 px','/brand/avatar-400.png'],['1000 px','/brand/avatar-1000.png']]},
];
const palette = [['Magpie blue','#004AAD'],['Ink','#172723'],['Paper','#FAFAF7'],['Surface','#F0F2ED'],['Muted','#63706A']];
const illustrations = [['Standing','magpie-standing'],['Looking back','magpie-looking-back'],['Flying','magpie-flying']];
const social = [['Wide banner','/brand/banner-1500x500.png'],['LinkedIn','/brand/banner-linkedin-1128x191.png'],['Bluesky','/brand/banner-bluesky-3000x1000.png']];
---
<ContentLayout title="Brand assets" description="The Magpie mark, illustrations, and visual language.">
 <section><h2>Logo</h2><p>Keep the original colors and proportions, with clear space around the mark. Use these assets when referring to Apache Magpie.</p><div class="brand-grid">{assets.map(asset=><div><a href={asset.image} class="asset-preview" download><img src={asset.image} alt={`Apache Magpie ${asset.name}`} loading="lazy"/></a><div class="asset-title">{asset.name}<span>{asset.links.map(([label,href])=><a href={href} download>{label} ↓</a>)}</span></div></div>)}</div></section>
 <section><h2>The bird</h2><div class="brand-grid">{illustrations.map(([name,file])=><div><a class="asset-preview" href={`/illustrations/magpie/${file}.png`} download><img src={`/illustrations/magpie/${file}.png`} alt={`Magpie ${name.toLowerCase()}`} loading="lazy"/></a><div class="asset-title">{name}<a href={`/illustrations/magpie/${file}.png`} download>PNG ↓</a></div></div>)}</div></section>
 <section><h2>Website palette</h2><div class="palette">{palette.map(([name,hex])=><div><div class="swatch" style={`background:${hex}`}></div><strong>{name}</strong><code>{hex}</code></div>)}</div><p>The preview pairs the original Magpie blue with quiet, warm surfaces. Blue marks actions; ink carries the content.</p></section>
 <section><h2>Typography</h2><p class="type-sample">More time for the work that matters.</p><p>Geist for headings, text, and controls. System monospace for code. Type stays upright, with weight and space providing the hierarchy.</p></section>
 <details><summary>Social banners</summary><div class="link-row">{social.map(([name,href])=><a href={href} download>{name} ↓</a>)}</div></details>
 <details><summary>Usage and licensing</summary><p>Assets are available under Apache License 2.0. Apache Magpie, Magpie, and Apache are trademarks of The Apache Software Foundation.</p><div class="link-row"><a href="https://www.apache.org/foundation/marks/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ASF trademark policy </a><a href="https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Apache License 2.0 </a></div></details>
</ContentLayout>
